{"ref":"BDB, יוֹנָה²","hw":"יוֹנָה²","html":"† II. <big><span dir=\"rtl\">יוֹנָה</span></big>  <strong>n.pr.m.</strong> prophet, according to <a data-ref=\"II Kings 14:25\" href=\"/II_Kings.14.25\">2 K 14:25</a> he was <span dir=\"rtl\">הַנָּבִיא</span>, son of <span dir=\"rtl\">אֲמִתַּי</span>, from <span dir=\"rtl\">גַּת הַחֵפֶר</span>, and predicted the recovery of Isr.’s territory which Jerob. II effected; he is also the principal figure of the Book of Jonah: <a data-ref=\"Jonah 1:1\" href=\"/Jonah.1.1\">1:1</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">(בֶּן־אֲמִתַּי)</span>, v <a data-ref=\"Jonah 1:3\" href=\"/Jonah.1.3\">3</a>, <a data-ref=\"Jonah 1:5\" href=\"/Jonah.1.5\">5</a>, <a data-ref=\"Jonah 1:7\" href=\"/Jonah.1.7\">7</a>, <a data-ref=\"Jonah 1:15\" href=\"/Jonah.1.15\">15</a> <a data-ref=\"Jonah 2:1\" href=\"/Jonah.2.1\">2:1</a><sup>(×2)</sup>, <a data-ref=\"Jonah 2:2\" href=\"/Jonah.2.2\">2</a>, <a data-ref=\"Jonah 2:11\" href=\"/Jonah.2.11\">11</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jonah 3:1\" href=\"/Jonah.3.1\">3:1</a>, <a data-ref=\"Jonah 3:3\" href=\"/Jonah.3.3\">3</a>, <a data-ref=\"Jonah 3:4\" href=\"/Jonah.3.4\">4</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jonah 4:1\" href=\"/Jonah.4.1\">4:1</a>, <a data-ref=\"Jonah 4:5\" href=\"/Jonah.4.5\">5</a>, <a data-ref=\"Jonah 4:6\" href=\"/Jonah.4.6\">6</a><sup>(×2)</sup>, <a data-ref=\"Jonah 4:8\" href=\"/Jonah.4.8\">8</a>, <a data-ref=\"Jonah 4:9\" href=\"/Jonah.4.9\">9</a>.","next":"BDB, יוֹנָה³","prev":"BDB, יוֹנָה"}